# D1b: wss://aldo.tech/demo/mqtt -> the demo bridge (127.0.0.1:18090). NOT APPLIED ANYWHERE.
#
# Put it into the (site) snippet of the Caddyfile, before the catch-all `handle` (the same place as the mirror's
# regions from scripts/mirror/caddy-apply.py), then:
#   caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile && systemctl reload caddy
# Taking it out again: delete the block, validate, reload. Only this path is proxied; /healthz of the bridge is
# not reachable from outside.
#
# Caddy upgrades WebSockets by itself. Because the client is not one of Caddy's trusted_proxies (do not add
# any), reverse_proxy REPLACES X-Forwarded-For with the real peer address, which is what the bridge counts
# per-address limits by. The bridge checks the Origin header itself.
	# BEGIN urMQTT demo bridge (D1b)
	handle /demo/mqtt {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:18090 {
			flush_interval -1
			header_down -Server
			transport http {
				dial_timeout 3s
				response_header_timeout 15s
			}
		}
	}
	# END urMQTT demo bridge
